  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Ask how someone is.",
   "texto": [
    "**Apa kabar?** is the usual formula to ask «How are you?» or «How are you?». Although **apa** means «what» and **kabar**, «news», it is not literally translated as «What news?» in this situation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Daily treatment",
   "texto": [
    "**Bapak** and **Ibu** serve to address adults with respect; they can also mean «Father» and «mother». **Mas** and **Mbak** are daily treatments for men and women, respectively, depending on the relationship and the situation. They do not always amount to «Sir.» and «Madam.» of Spanish."
   ]
  },
